# rm397, the missing bench (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm397
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for cty_linden_sedgeditch
written_by codex
title the missing bench
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=sailor temper=calm
traits temper=calm talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=dry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk counts_empty_places_first_and_sums_the_moving_ones_later
likes crisp_apples long_walks market_bustle first_snow
dislikes flies salt_wind
fears a_head_count_that_misses_one_quiet_passenger
hopes a_walk_with_nothing_left_to_count
topics ships +0.5 travel +0.5 pastimes +0.4 animals -0.2
styles comfort=room gossip=quiet refuse=patient tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# counts empty places under the breath before counting anything in motion and regards a clear patch of bench as an unusually reliable witness.

words
oath! = A bench adrift | Five spare elbows
saying! = Count the quiet gap twice | An empty seat stays counted
place = the spare place | a broad gap
thwart = a boat bench | the cross seat
cord = a short painter | the mooring line
step = a low footboard | the boarding step
loadbag = a soft bundle | the lashed sack
apple = a crisp little apple | one sharp green apple
score = my quiet score | the muttered count
heel = the waiting heel | a wet heelprint
shelter = the lee seat | a corner beyond the draught
snowband = a pale rim | a cap of first snow
fly = a brisk nuisance | a harrying fly
turn = the outer circuit | my unhurried route

any
opinion @1 houses mixed 0 : There's no advantage in putting a House crest on a bench. It still only takes so many backsides.
opinion @1 merchants for 1 : I enjoy the sound of a market in full business. Every seller has a claim and sometimes one even has an apple to match.
opinion @1 church mixed 0 : A little room left on a bench does quiet credit to the first arrival.
opinion @1 dole for 1 : A share laid out for a latecomer costs rather less than an evening explaining why none remains.
opinion @1 road for 2 : After a stretch afloat a long walk offers the considerable pleasure of ground that stays where it was put.
opinion @1 watch mixed 0 : I'd go for a count of actual empty seats before asking several excited witnesses how many sailed.

grown
line @1 greet : Here's a free place. Hello to you. | Welcome. You've saved me counting that gap.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : I don't recall that face among the seated yet. | First meeting. Have yourself a bit of room.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. The unoccupied places are still in the majority. | Early feet and an agreeable amount of elbow room.
line @1 greet.return : Heard you. I was just finishing with the gaps. | Hello returned without changing the total.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : A familiar face fills the place rather nicely. | You've come within counting distance again.
line @3 greet.return [here.time=night] : Late hello. I do a fair amount by ear now. | Evening has thinned the company out considerably.
line @1 again.open : I seem to have accounted for you twice now. | We've met again without the space being measurably larger.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : There's a place with your name very conspicuously absent. | Come stand where the moving bits look interesting.
line @1 farewell : Walk comfortably while the ground permits it. | May a dry seat await you when the travelling's done.
line @1 farewell.return : I'll mark the space empty when you've gone. | Take a comfortable piece of quiet along.
line @1 react.news : I've interrupted a much less interesting count for your news. | Let the tale arrive in its own good time.
line @1 react.news.new : That didn't appear in my earlier count. | Entirely new company for my thoughts.
line @1 react.news.known : I've counted those particulars once before. | Yes. It occupies about the same space as the earlier report.
line @1 react.news.doubt : There's an empty place halfway through your account. | I can count several claims and rather fewer facts.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|crime|assault|loss|theft] : Leave your things here and sit a good while. | Heavy hearing. No reason for you to take it straight off again.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|work] : Now there's news worth making extra room for. | I'd give that a very satisfactory place on today's count.
line @1 ask.how : How's the room about you today? | Managed to get a comfortable seat anywhere?
line @1 answer.how : Still afloat this end, broadly speaking. | My count is modest and my appetite sound.
line @1 decline : I'd be pencilling in a place that's already promised elsewhere. | I can't see enough clear space in my day to do that properly.
line @1 accept_decline : An empty place is admirably easy to record. | Fair. I'll leave the space quite clear.
line @1 preclose : I should move on before sitting becomes my whole occupation. | I'd like to walk while there's a little room ahead.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go on. No fare due for the seat. | Your place will probably continue to exist without you.
line @1 thank : You saved me from counting everybody a third time. Thanks. | I value a helping paw that knows where it will fit.
line @1 deflect_thanks : I had room enough to shift along. | Didn't alter the count by more than a comfortable fraction.
line @1 sympathise : This place remains yours till you feel ready to move. | No need to explain why you'd like to sit quietly.
line @1 reassure : Let's count what we have left before dining on worry. | A little breathing space can often be found sideways.
line @1 ack : I see how that total came about. | Yes. The spare place agrees with you.
line @1 give.advice : Count the still things before the lively ones. | Leave a bit of bench unoccupied till the last bundle's aboard.
scene quietgap
when topic=ships self.job=sailor
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An empty bench will sit admirably still for a count.
b : Not when the boat rolls. | Why count an empty bit?
a : Quite. But it won't generally take an interest in another bench halfway through. | To check against the number aboard. Two counts approach the same business from opposite ends.

scene bagsit
when topic=work self.job=sailor self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A parcel sitting quietly on a seat can lead to an alarming surplus of passengers on paper.
b : Surely you'd notice the parcel? | Does it count as empty or occupied?
a : I should hope so. I look for the feet below before declaring a cargo sack a tourist. | Occupied space with no passenger. Two columns prevent a great deal of confusion.

scene edgefloat
when topic=ships self.job=sailor
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I prefer an empty finger's width between the last seated wolf and an edge. | My idea of a full boat allows a little movement without an argument.
b : Would you leave another passenger behind? | How much movement?
a : I'd wait or shift things honestly. Claiming an imaginary seat helps nobody travel. | Enough to turn a shoulder without bringing the whole neighbourhood along.

scene walkshore
when topic=travel self.likes=long_walks
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : On foot I enjoy a stationary bank and the satisfaction of providing my own movement.
b : Seems the same sort of movement. | Ever wish for a ride back?
a : My legs have a quite distinct opinion about the difference. | Often. Then I sit awhile and discover legs will vote differently after an apple.

scene busyplace
when topic=pastimes self.likes=market_bustle
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At a busy market you can count the stalls by watching where all the gaps disappear.
b : You actually enjoy the crush? | Looking for a bargain?
a : I enjoy it best from a little outside the thick part. The bustle can do the hard labour. | A green apple and free entertainment. Some days the same stall provides both.

scene crispapple
when topic=food self.likes=crisp_apples
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An apple fresh enough to crack cleanly buys me a quiet interval.
b : How long an interval? | Quiet with all that crunching?
a : A bite, a chew and time to consider whether the present question requires an answer. | For conversation, yes. The apple may make its own remarks.

scene saltface
when topic=weather self.dislikes=salt_wind
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Salt wind gets far too grand an account in certain songs. | I approve of the sea right up to the bit that arrives on my nose.
b : It sounds romantic. | Would you rather sail in still air?
a : I can't hear romance through the sound of my eyes watering. | A breeze is useful. I'd take the propelling service without the extra seasoning.

scene snowseats
when topic=weather here.weather=snow
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Fresh snow declares every empty bench with admirable impartiality.
b : Can you tell the duration of the vacancy? | Not everyone wants to sit in snow.
a : My knowledge begins and ends with the snow. Since it fell, roughly. | That's a gap with a reasonably plain explanation. A dry cloth might adjust the answer.

scene fliesroll
when topic=animals self.dislikes=flies
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I never count flies. One possesses all the inconvenience usually attributed to a dozen.
b : Would knowing the number help? | What if there's only one?
a : Only if I could enter the lot in a book and shut it on them. | Then it's a remarkably diligent specimen and I wish it a long career elsewhere.

scene flowmarket
when topic=prices
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : A gap where a fine crate of apples stood is information. It doesn't prove they were cheap.
b : They all sold, didn't they? | What else would you check?
a : Or went back on a cart. I saw the gap, not the money changing paws. | A buyer willing to share the price. The crate itself has become rather unavailable.

scene welcomebank
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A newcomer offered a seat generally tells a clearer story about the road. | I keep a bench end open for a new arrival to choose an end.
b : Which end would you choose? | Expecting a story in exchange?
a : The sheltered one. An appeal that becomes rather obvious after a sea breeze. | No. That's part of what leaves the conversation so pleasant when it does arrive.

scene quietfriend
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd trust #self.friend# to remind me the walk ought to go somewhere. | I can enjoy a long interval on a seat beside #self.friend#.
b : Would you go too quickly? | How long's a long interval?
a : Quite the reverse in an interesting market. I'd start counting all the gaps again. | Long enough for each of us to decide about another apple. I'm in no desperate hurry.

scene housewhisper
when topic=gossip
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : An unoccupied bench can keep several exceedingly grand secrets without effort.
b : Do you mean a particular secret? | You could sit and tell me one.
a : I mean the useful example set by the bench. | I could sit and join it in remaining quiet. That's what I have in mind.

scene quietprayer
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In my prayer after a crossing I remember the quiet passenger as carefully as the loud company.
b : Can a passenger escape your count? | You pray for all aboard?
a : On one count, certainly. I try to make sure the last look includes the easy-to-miss places. | It takes no extra weight aboard to wish every one of the party home in peace.

scene leanferry
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Sparse company at a stall can hide a surprising number of empty purses at home.
b : So you wouldn't judge a week's trade by the crowd? | Do you count the quiet gaps there too?
a : Not without asking somebody who had been making actual sales. | I notice them. I'd need to hear the reasons before presuming to speak for an entire street.

scene shelterdream
when topic=dreams
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My perfect evening ends with a seat to spare without any more arithmetic expected. | I'd like a walk that ends before my legs propose a vote on the route.
b : Where's your ideal resting place? | Would you pick the short route?
a : Where I'd have a crisp apple to eat and surf providing the music. | A different one. Familiar ground tends to include too many interesting things to inspect.

scene drizzleland
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A light rain alters the market count considerably faster than the town population. | The number of occupied awnings goes up exactly when the uncovered benches go empty.
b : Where does everybody shelter? | Does rain bother your calculations?
a : Under the deepest overhangs. Somebody sells shelter very successfully without charging for it. | It simply adds a column for moving sideways at a brisk pace.

scene latecart
when topic=caravan world.wagons=late
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An overdue wagon gives an excellent opportunity to observe the difference between empty space and free time.
b : How so? | You can sit, can't you?
a : An empty place in the yard and a day spent waiting aren't equally available for use. | Certainly. It's a borrowed seat when my mind remains harnessed to the missing wagon.

story applecount [topic=food|memories]
  : I bought several apples, counted them in my bag and ate one on the way home. When I counted again there was still the same number.
  : Turned out the largest apple had been sitting in the bottom fold where I'd missed it.
  b : A free apple, then?
  : A paid apple and an entirely free lesson about folded cloth.

story silentbench [topic=work|memories self.job=sailor]
  : I once remarked on a passenger's remarkable patience while I finished a small count. A bundled coat never shifted an inch on the bench.
  : No feet beneath. No ears above. An unusually economical traveller.
  b : Did you charge the coat?
  : I moved it onto a bundle. Its fare was more than adequately covered by the subsequent saving in seat space.

story wrongwalk [topic=travel|memories]
  : I went for a walk promising myself I wouldn't count anything. During my return I felt very pleased with how well I'd done.
  : I caught myself counting the number of corners where I'd resisted temptation.
  b : A successful outing anyway?
  : Entirely. I went out on two legs and returned on the agreed number without having to recount them.

rule @gap
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Count the clear bit before it fills with somebody's hat. | One uncovered spot. That's a useful beginning.

rule @work
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=sailor
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Bundles down where they won't acquire passenger status, please. | Look under that coat for a pair of feet before confirming the count.

rule @apple
when concept=bark self.likes=crisp_apples
does aside
cooldown 8h
say An excellent crack to that bite. No further commentary needed. | One apple for the walk and a spare in case the road proves interesting.

rule @rain
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Wipe this end first if you mean to sit. | The sheltered seat has become unexpectedly popular.

dlg @1 resident.hub : I've finished with the empty spaces and would gladly hear from one that's occupied.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, your arrival always calls for a modest adjustment to my arithmetic.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : After dark I let footfalls to stand in temporarily for the view.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Take the end of the bench if you mean to ask. The gap between us is free too.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=sailor] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I'd give a spare seat a second look before promising it to anybody.
dlg @2 resident.job : My work generally improves when every empty place has been noticed.
dlg @1 resident.bye : I hope there's a dry bit of bench waiting beyond the last mile.
graft resident.hub
choice How can an empty seat help you count passengers? -> gapcount
node gapcount
say First count seats without any wolf in them, then account for the parcels. It's a check on the moving heads. One head may take a lively interest in three seats.
free
choice Does that always give the right answer? -> headagain
choice I'll watch the parcels. -> hub
node headagain
say If both answers agree I take a last look. If they differ, I take two. The system has yet to produce an extra traveller merely because I wrote one down.
choice I'll take the extra look. -> hub
choice Goodbye from one occupied place. -> bye
